GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/memory_rw.c:156:  *    - post-#430 it fires only on PHYSICAL accesses.  A TRANSLATED 4096-byte write across a
GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/memory_rw.c:157:  *      1 MB boundary is chunked at the 1024-byte SPLIT granule, so it costs 4 translations
GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/memory_rw.c:158:  *      and 4 host lookups and never reaches here; PHYSICAL costs 0 and 2.  A chunk of at
GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/memory_rw.c:159:  *      most one granule, granule-aligned, cannot cross 1 MB.
GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/memory_rw.c:160:  *    - its head can NEVER be a device, in either version: device dispatch `goto
GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/memory_rw.c:161:  *      do_return_ok`s first.  Measured with a device straddling the memblock boundary --
GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/memory_rw.c:162:  *      one device call, offset 0xffe, len 4, zero host lookups.
GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/memory_rw.c:163:  *
