GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/memory_rw.c:165:  *  does NOT eliminate the tail call -- measured at -O0, 1,834,896 bytes of stack for a 16 MB
GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/memory_rw.c:166:  *  access -- and a large enough access then dies on the stack rather than returning an
GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/memory_rw.c:167:  *  answer.
GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/memory_rw.c:168:  *
GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/memory_rw.c:169:  *  CORRECTION, and it is the reason this paragraph is worded carefully: the first draft said
